cff-version: 1.2.0
title: FastXeBench
message: "If you use this repository, please cite the FastXeBench paper and link to the public artifact."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Xu
    given-names: Zirui
    affiliation: Nanjing Normal University
    email: 19230444@njnu.edu.cn
repository-code: "https://github.com/handsomeZR-netizen/fastxebench"
abstract: >-
  FastXeBench is a reproducible benchmark and fidelity study of edit-to-PDF
  latency for XeLaTeX on Windows. It combines workload-aware benchmarking,
  a prime-plus-measure protocol for incremental edits, and explicit PDF
  fidelity checks.
keywords:
  - xelatex
  - benchmark
  - reproducibility
  - windows
  - latexmk
  - performance
license: MIT
